<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alfred-Amédée Dodds</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1842–1922</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alfred-Amédée Dodds was a French general of mixed African and European descent, born at Saint-Louis in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senegal">Senegal</a>. He commanded the French expedition of 1892 in the Second Franco-Dahomean War, defeating the army of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/behanzin">Béhanzin</a> and taking the capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abomey">Abomey</a>; Béhanzin surrendered in 1894 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-dahomey">Dahomey</a> became a French colony. Dodds later commanded French forces in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indochina">Indochina</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alfred-amedee-dodds.jpg" alt="Alfred-Amédée Dodds" width="320" height="435" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Charles Ogereau (1868-1908) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:General_Dodds_in_1902.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
